# Rust
target/

# Tauri regenerates these from the capability manifests on every build.
desktop/gen/schemas/

# Node / frontend
node_modules/
dist/

# Astro's generated types and build cache, under site/. Regenerated on every
# `astro dev` and `astro build`; tsconfig.json references the types file, which
# is why a fresh checkout has to run one of those before `astro check` passes.
.astro/

# The development wiki. RHIZOLOG_ROOT defaults to ./wiki, so running the
# backend creates this: scratch content plus a derived SQLite index under
# .rhizolog/. None of it belongs in the repo.
backend/wiki/

# Rhizolog's own files inside any wiki directory, including example-wiki/.
# The index is built from the markdown beside it and rebuilds on startup;
# server.json says where a running server is listening and means nothing once
# that server stops.
#
# By name, not the whole directory: `.rhizolog/times/`, `.rhizolog/ideas/` and
# `.rhizolog/words/` sit beside them and are a time log, an idea inbox and a
# writing history, all three authored data with no other copy. A wiki kept in
# git should ignore these lines and nothing more.
#
# `**/` because a pattern with a slash in it is anchored to this file's own
# directory: plain `.rhizolog/index.db` would miss `example-wiki/`'s.
**/.rhizolog/index.db
**/.rhizolog/index.db-*
**/.rhizolog/server.json

# Accounts. Authored data with no other copy, like the time log, and unlike the
# time log, secret: each file carries an Argon2 hash of a real password. Not
# reversible, and still not a thing to commit. Back the directory up; do not
# push it. See knowledge-base/accounts.md.
**/.rhizolog/users/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.log

# Except the word log, which this file very nearly threw away. `.rhizolog/words/`
# is authored data with no other copy and is meant to be committed, and the rule
# above is not anchored, so it matches a `.log` file at any depth. The negation
# works because no *directory* on the way to it is excluded; if `.rhizolog/` ever
# becomes an ignored directory, this line stops meaning anything and git will not
# say so. See knowledge-base/long-form.md.
!**/.rhizolog/words/*.log
